  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Revising Project Scope**\n\nI\'m now completely rethinking the approach. The initial React app idea is out. We\'re pivoting to a single HTML file prototype as requested. It needs Tailwind CSS via CDN, vanilla JS, PapaParse, and Chart.js or Plotly. This changes everything, focusing on a rapid, lightweight deliverable.\n\n\n**Considering Implementation Path**\n\nI\'m now weighing the best path forward, given the React/Vite environment. While the user\'s focus on a single HTML file is clear, I\'m considering either replacing `index.html` with a complete HTML prototype or building within the React environment but providing a similar single-page experience. Given the guidelines, using React and Recharts seems the more efficient route to achieve an interactive dashboard. The user instructions specifically require \"a complete, single-file HTML prototype,\" so I am reconsidering the single-HTML file solution.\n\n\n"
