    thinking: "**Initiating React App Build**\n\nI\'m starting on the React application. The immediate plan is the foundational structure. I\'m building out a header, titled \"Bolivia Synthetic CPI Tracker\", with a helpful tooltip that explains the methodology used, a matched-model Jevons calculation, that filters out temporada categories. Next, I\'ll be working on the navigation, laying out tabs for the National level, followed by La Paz, Cochabamba, Santa Cruz, and a Live Product section.\n\n\n**Constructing Chart Components**\n\nI\'m now focused on the visualizations. I\'m planning out the charts: a national CPI line chart with city toggles, then individual city charts with category toggles, and finally a Live Product count graph. I\'m going to include download buttons for the CSV data below each visualization.\n\nI\'m also working on parsing the CSVs asynchronously with a custom hook to manage data fetching and parsing using PapaParse. I\'m figuring out the best way to load the CSV data, either on demand per tab, or loading all the data in a context. The immediate plan is to load the data asynchronously when the dashboard mounts. I\'ve also identified the data sources.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 172648349
    }
