  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Implementing Zoom Functionality**\n\nI\'m currently focused on implementing a zoom slider using the `Brush` component from `Recharts` for our charts. My initial thought is to place this slider at the bottom of each chart, which would allow users to zoom in on specific date ranges. However, since we have multiple charts in each view (like CPI Timeline and Inflation Rate), I\'m considering whether to synchronize them or simply add a brush to the bottom of each one.\n\n\n**Verifying Sync Functionality**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that `recharts`\'s `syncId` attribute does, in fact, synchronize the `Brush` component across multiple charts! I\'m now implementing this across views. I\'m adding `syncId` props (e.g., `\"nationalViewSync\"`) to the `LineChart` and `AreaChart` components within each view, so they share zoom state and tooltips. The `Brush` itself will be added to the bottom chart of each view, except for the `ProductCountView` which has only one chart.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 806208308
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
