  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Date Visualization**\n\nI\'m currently focused on improving the display of \"forward fill\" dates on the X-axis. Instead of directly altering the Line\'s dots, I\'m considering adding a separate visual indicator for these dates, potentially through markers, highlights using `ReferenceArea`, or a similar approach on the X-axis itself. This aims for clearer distinction.\n\n\n**Exploring X-Axis Highlighting**\n\nI\'m now exploring approaches beyond basic `ReferenceArea` and `ReferenceLine` for highlighting forward-fill dates. The potential for numerous dates makes these options less ideal. My latest thought is to modify the XAxis `tick` rendering. While this seemed promising, the limited rendering based on generated ticks poses a challenge. I\'m also considering a custom component for the XAxis tick or adding a `Scatter` or `Line` and clamping the data.\n\n\n**Considering Visual Anchoring**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a new idea: using a modified visual element tied to the X-axis for \"forward fill\" date indication. I\'m considering using a hidden `Bar` or `Line` and changing the shape, or an `AreaChart` element, or a `ReferenceLine` element on the timeline. A custom `XAxis` `tick` component seemed promising at first, but is now less likely to work as intended. I\'m also considering creating a custom `<ReferenceDot>`, but I need to make sure the data is properly passed.\n\n\n**Investigating Coordinate Retrieval**\n\nI\'m now grappling with getting the exact coordinates for the drawing area within the chart. I need to know the bottom, but Recharts doesn\'t directly pass `yAxis` properties. I\'m considering using `cx` and `cy` data for this and the best approach now seems to be drawing a marker on the X-axis inside `ForwardFillDot`. I\'m also exploring using an extra `Scatter` or `Line` component visually placed on the x-axis, with a specific marker field. I\'m hoping this will provide a clear visual.\n\n\n**Evaluating X-Axis Markers**\n\nI\'m now back at the idea of using the XAxis, specifically its `tick` element. The key is to overcome the limitation of sampled ticks. The goal is to highlight *all* forward-fill dates, not just those coinciding with tick generation. A custom XAxis `tick` component with conditional rendering seems like the best approach, though I\'m still trying to get the right visual. The earlier ideas with `Scatter` or `ReferenceLine` seem simpler than originally thought. I am now considering a `<Brush>` tick.\n\n\n**Implementing ReferenceLines**\n\nI\'ve returned to the `ReferenceLine` approach, but am changing the design. I\'m focusing on rendering a large number of these elements; the SVG is fast enough. The challenge is in the visual presentation. I\'m testing using a very light, potentially dashed line, a `segment` or a small thick marker on the x-axis, instead of a full line, and am not using `y1` or `y2`. A custom `shape` on an `Area` or `Bar` that only renders a notch is now another option.\n\nI\'m now back at the idea of using the XAxis, specifically its `tick` element. The key is to overcome the limitation of sampled ticks. The goal is to highlight *all* forward-fill dates, not just those coinciding with tick generation. A custom XAxis `tick` component with conditional rendering seems like the best approach, though I\'m still trying to get the right visual. The earlier ideas with `Scatter` or `ReferenceLine` seem simpler than originally thought. I am now considering a `<Brush>` tick.\n\n\n**Testing Scatter Plot Approach**\n\nI\'m now investigating a hidden `Scatter` chart on a secondary Y-axis. The data point\'s `shape` will render a rectangle. I\'m also considering `ReferenceArea` for continuous date ranges. My current priority is determining the best way to visually highlight *specific* dates, as indicated by user needs. I\'m exploring an x-axis marker using a `<Scatter>` plot.\n\n\n**Verifying Marker Coordinates**\n\nI\'m now very optimistic about the `<Scatter>` chart approach. By setting a hidden secondary `YAxis` with a domain of `[0, 1]` and plotting markers at `y=0`, I can ensure they\'re *precisely* on the X-axis. The `shape` prop within the Scatter component offers direct control to ensure the markers are at the bottom of the chart.\n\n\n**Refining Date Marking**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `<Scatter>` plot method, drawing a shape using `circle` or `<rect>` for markers. By using `y=0` on a hidden secondary `YAxis`, I\'m confident they\'ll sit right on the X-axis. Although `Scatter` relies on `ComposedChart`, modifying from `LineChart` to `ComposedChart` is easy! I\'m now certain the marker will properly display.\n\n\n**Implementing Area-Based Marking**\n\nI\'m now implementing the \"rug plot\" concept using a hidden `YAxis` and `Area` component. I\'m using a `markerValue` data key that is 0.05 if it\'s forward fill data, 0 otherwise, and then use that data point to draw a histogram on the X-axis. This approach allows a flexible visual indicator. I\'m now making sure all other components use the correct `yAxisId`.\n\n\n**Evaluating Bar Chart Technique**\n\nI\'m now implementing a \"rug plot\" visualization using a `Bar` chart in a `ComposedChart`. A hidden secondary Y-axis drives a \"markerValue\" data key to be 0.05 for forward-fill dates and 0 otherwise. This drives the display of a bar-shaped marker directly on the X-axis. I\'m checking existing chart instances and integrating the `Bar` plot on all relevant charts. This has proven to be an effective visual indicator.\n\n\n**Confirming Visual Implementation**\n\nNow I\'m verifying the \"rug plot\" implementation using the `ComposedChart` structure with a hidden `YAxis`. The main chart data, `XAxis`, and `YAxis` all remain as before, but I\'ve seamlessly integrated a `Bar` plot driven by a \"markerValue\" key to highlight forward-fill dates. This confirms the new solution, with no modifications needed to the existing chart.\n\n\n"
