  user_input {
    user_response: "for the \"!\" popup: This tracker provides a high-frequency, synthetic price index based exclusively on daily supermarket retail data. While the categorization and weighting methodology is benchmarked against the official Instituto Nacional de Estad\303\255stica (INE) framework, this is not a complete Consumer Price Index (CPI). It focuses on a \"Core-5\" basket of retail goods (representing roughly 49% of official weights) and structurally excludes non-retail inflation drivers such as housing, transportation, healthcare services, and utilities. It should be used as a supplementary indicator of retail price trends rather than a replacement for official macroeconomic data.\nApply style changes to the selected element(s).\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nCSS selector 1: div#root:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > header:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > svg:nth-of-type(1)\nCSS 1: {\n\n}\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    items {
      text: "for the \"!\" popup: This tracker provides a high-frequency, synthetic price index based exclusively on daily supermarket retail data. While the categorization and weighting methodology is benchmarked against the official Instituto Nacional de Estad\303\255stica (INE) framework, this is not a complete Consumer Price Index (CPI). It focuses on a \"Core-5\" basket of retail goods (representing roughly 49% of official weights) and structurally excludes non-retail inflation drivers such as housing, transportation, healthcare services, and utilities. It should be used as a supplementary indicator of retail price trends rather than a replacement for official macroeconomic data.\nApply style changes to the selected element(s).\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nCSS selector 1: div#root:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > header:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > svg:nth-of-type(1)\nCSS 1: {\n\n}\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
